From f989b936eea8aecb3bad931028ed62e499761cb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 03:15:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Sweep: system/feature/help types + Layout.LayoutEngine
 namespace fix

Additive support types (signatures from the net48 reference):

- WindowsFormsSynchronizationContext : SynchronizationContext, marshalling Post/Send
  onto the GTK main loop via Gtk.Application.Invoke so async continuations resume on
  the UI thread. (Send is for cross-thread use; calling it from the UI thread would
  deadlock, as in WinForms.)
- OSFeature/FeatureSupport/IFeatureSupport - feature detection; no Windows features
  are reported present on GTK.
- PowerStatus (+ PowerLineStatus/BatteryChargeStatus enums) - defaults to
  unknown / no-system-battery where no power API is wired.
- Help (static, no-op display boundary) and HelpProvider (an IExtenderProvider that
  stores per-control help strings/keywords/navigators/show-help).
- SystemParameter enum.

Also fixes the LayoutEngine namespace: the empty System.Windows.Forms.LayoutEngine
placeholder is moved to System.Windows.Forms.Layout.LayoutEngine (the real
namespace) with InitLayout/Layout, and the three referencing files import it. This
unblocks `using System.Windows.Forms.Layout;` code.

Net48 public types present 859->870 (missing 175->164). Full suite green at 2335
(+6 tests).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
